<%#
  Setting somebody up who has no account.

  Two fields, and neither of them is an email address. That absence is the
  design rather than an omission: with no address there is no lookup, so this
  form cannot be used to find out who already has an account, and the person
  being set up never has to find a message in an inbox and trust a link inside
  it — the exact interaction this audience is warned never to trust.

  The copy is deliberately plain about what happens next, because a caregiver
  who does not know the care receiver has to agree will read the empty activity
  panel as a bug.
%>
<div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto space-y-6">
  <div>
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900">Set up someone you care for</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
      They do not need an email address or an account. You write the reminders;
      they open a link on their tablet or computer once, and it stays open.
    </p>
  </div>

  <%= form_with url: care_receivers_path, method: :post, scope: :user, class: "bg-white shadow rounded-lg p-6 space-y-5" do |f| %>
    <div>
      <%= f.label :name, "Their name", class: "block text-sm font-medium text-gray-700" %>
      <%= f.text_field :name, value: @senior&.name, required: true, autofocus: true,
            placeholder: "Mum",
            class: "mt-1 w-full border border-gray-300 rounded-md shadow-sm py-2 px-3 focus:ring-blue-500 focus:border-blue-500" %>
      <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-gray-500">
        What Remindly will call them, on screen and out loud.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <%= f.label :tz, "Their timezone", class: "block text-sm font-medium text-gray-700" %>
      <%# Theirs, not yours. Reminders are expanded in this zone, so a caregiver
          three timezones away who leaves their own here would have every dose
          fire at the wrong hour — the clock bug this project has already had
          twice. %>
      <%= f.select :tz,
            options_for_select(current_user.timezone_options, @senior&.tz || current_user.tz),
            {},
            class: "mt-1 w-full border border-gray-300 rounded-md shadow-sm py-2 px-3 focus:ring-blue-500 focus:border-blue-500" %>
      <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-gray-500">
        Where they live, not where you are. Reminder times follow their clock.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="rounded-md bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 p-4">
      <p class="text-sm text-blue-900">
        <strong>They have the final say.</strong> You can write reminders straight
        away, but nothing is spoken and you will see no activity until they open
        the link and agree. If they decline, the account is deleted.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
      <%= f.submit "Set them up",
            class: "inline-flex items-center px-4 py-2 border border-transparent text-sm font-medium rounded-md text-white bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-700 cursor-pointer" %>
      <%= link_to "Cancel", dashboard_path, class: "text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-gray-900" %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
